The published checkpoints are files of the same repository and carry no
separate terms, so they are under its licence: BSD-3-Clause at the commit above
(Apache-2.0 when they were committed, in 2022 and 2023). OpenCV Zoo distributes
the "small" network (yunet_s) as face_detection_yunet_2023mar.onnx under the MIT
License. They were trained on WIDER FACE, with the landmark annotations SCRFD
published; the dataset's own terms (non-commercial research) govern the dataset.

The five landmark names in the published labels.json are OpenCV's, from the
FaceDetectorYN documentation (right eye, left eye, nose tip, right and left
corner of the mouth), in the order the checkpoints' landmark channels emit them.

